text:
First of all i'd like to mention I am running 2 bridges and 1 relay. I am new to this, and as much as I've tinkered with linux over the years I consider myself still a noobie.

&amp;#x200B;

I created my standalone snowflake on fedora last night, but i seem to get no traffic and the error logs seems to be indicating certain things that I can't tell if it is normal or not.

First of all if anyone could answer any questions

Can I nickname my snowflake as to see certain details on tor relay search. (in torrc)

Which port should typically be open? ( I opened 32768-60999 on UDP)

Can I set Contactinfo in torrc.

I tried setting my tor.service to point to the torrc in the snowflake/client however it fails to start consistently, can anyone share any thoughts on how to get this to work, or where I might see an actual error message to help me out with the resolution. Starting it manually and need to leave open the window seems a bit odd. tor -f torrc does work.

selinux is turned off.

&amp;#x200B;

Is this normal from the log file ?

